<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rivas, Nicaragua</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rivas is a city in south-western Nicaragua, capital of the Rivas <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>, on the narrow isthmus between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-nicaragua">Lake Nicaragua</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a>. The area was home to the Nahua-speaking Nicarao, whose ruler met the Spanish conquistador <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gil-gonzalez-davila">Gil González Dávila</a> in 1523. During the National War, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-walker">William Walker</a>'s filibusters fought battles at Rivas in 1855 and 1856 and surrendered there on 1 May 1857.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rivas-nicaragua.jpg" alt="Rivas, Nicaragua" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: jessicadally · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Street_in_Rivas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
